    "probe_text": "The controller method confirms the sequence. Here is the complete ordered list.\n\n# POST `/api/owners` \u2014 validations & side-effects, in order\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Before the method body (framework layer)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`. (Enforced only when `petclinic.security.enable=true`; inert under the disable-security config.)\n\n2. **Bean Validation (JSR-380)** on the `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` \u2014 all constraints evaluated together:\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull` + `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words) + `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull` + `@Pattern` (letters, optional trailing `.`) + `@Size(1..30)`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull` + `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull` + `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull` + `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate`: `@Valid` (optional)\n   - `postcode`: no JSR-380 constraint\n\n3. **Custom `OwnerFieldsValidator`** (registered via `@InitBinder`, same `@Valid` pass), which runs in this internal order:\n   1. **Normalizes `address` in place** (trim, collapse spaces, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE) \u2014 a mutation that happens *before* the required check.\n   2. **Required non-blank check** on firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone \u2192 error `\"required\"`.\n   3. **Telephone** \u2192 `toE164` normalization/validation (assumes `+61`, drops leading 0, enforces per-country digit counts); writes canonical value back, or error `\"telephone.invalid\"`.\n   4. **Email** (optional) \u2192 regex check; lower-cased back into DTO, or error `\"email.invalid\"`.\n   5. **Postcode** (optional) \u2192 must be a 4-digit code valid for the city's region (NSW/VIC/QLD tables; unknown city \u2192 any 4 digits), or error `\"postcode.invalid\"`.\n\n   Any error from step 2 or 3 \u2192 **400** and the create is aborted before the method runs.\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Inside `addOwner` (business validations interleaved with side-effects)\n\nEach numbered item runs in this exact source order (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:175\u2013200`). Side-effects marked **[S]**, aborting validations marked **[V]**:\n\n4. **[S]** Map DTO \u2192 `Owner` entity (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`; ignores id, pets, householdId; `sharesHousehold` not mapped).\n5. **[S]** **Assign registration date** \u2014 supplied date or `now(clock)`, then rolled to a business day (Sat/Sun \u2192 Mon). Mutates `owner.registrationDate`.\n6. **[V]** **City-capacity check** \u2014 if owners in that city `>= 50` \u2192 **409 Conflict**, no save.\n7. **[V]** **Daily-limit check** \u2014 if owners with that registration date `>= 100` \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**, no save.\n8. **[S]** **Household assignment** \u2014 only if `sharesHousehold == true` **and** a duplicate household (same normalized last name + address) exists: sets `owner.householdId` (SHA-256-derived 12-hex id) **and back-fills + saves existing household members** that lack a householdId (persists *other* owner rows).\n9. **[V]** **Identity-duplicate check** \u2014 if any existing owner shares identity key `telephone|email|householdId` \u2192 **409 Conflict**, no save.\n10. **[S]** **Household size** \u2014 sets `householdSize` = members with same householdId + 1 (else 1).\n11. **[S]** **Customer code** \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `CITY3-LAST3-NNNN` where NNNN = cityCount + 1.\n12. **[S]** **Namesake count** \u2014 sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners with same first+last (case-insensitive).\n13. **[S]** **Membership level** \u2014 base 1, +1 if email present, +1 if namesakeCount == 0, capped at 3.\n14. **[S]** **Bulk-signup warning** \u2014 `true` if owners on that registration date `> 80`.\n15. **[S]** **Persist** \u2014 `saveOwner` \u2192 `em.persist` INSERT; DB generates the id (own `@Transactional` per service call; the controller is not transactional).\n16. **[S]** **Audit log** \u2014 one INFO line to the `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n17. **[S]** **Build 201 response** \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\n## Notably absent on this path\n- No password encoding (BCrypt exists only for the auth `users` table, unrelated).\n- No application events published, no emails/messaging.\n- No child entities created \u2014 pets are ignored by the mapper. The only writes to *other* rows are the household back-fill in step 8.\n\nOne thing worth flagging: several checks in Phase 2 (capacity, daily limit, identity/household duplicates, namesake, customer code) rely on `findAllOwners()` / count queries executed in separate transactions from the final `saveOwner`, so they are read-then-write with no locking \u2014 susceptible to races under concurrent creates. You asked me only to read and report, so I've changed nothing."
